2026-09-10T14:28:03.7484767Z > 🤖 **SPARQ agent** — automated HEAVY-set drift alarm (scripts/heavy_set_alarm.py, bead sq-6vshe.7). @jeswr runs multiple agents on this account; this issue was filed by CI automation.
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7485794Z 
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7486092Z <!-- heavy-set-alarm-key: ci.yml:jobs.test.env.HEAVY -->
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7486405Z 
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7487112Z `.github/workflows/ci.yml` `jobs.test.env.HEAVY` is the single source of truth for the load-aware shard matrix. A measured full-workspace run disagrees with it:
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7487695Z 
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7488409Z * **UNDECLARED** `newly_slow` (55.0s) — measured heavy but NOT in `HEAVY` — it is running inside a bulk shard right now, re-skewing the load-aware split
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7488932Z 
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7489093Z Heavy floor: **20s** (demotion floor 10s).
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7489293Z 
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7491299Z **Fix**: for an UNDECLARED test, add `| test(=its_name)` to `HEAVY` and — if it is comparable to the existing heavies — give it its own `matrix.include` shard (the bulk filter is the negation of `HEAVY`, so it re-narrows automatically). For a MISSING one, update the atom to the test's current name or drop it along with its shard. For a DEMOTED one, drop it from `HEAVY` and delete its shard so the parallelism goes back to the bulk split.
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7492701Z 
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7493451Z Left alone, the shards stop finishing together and the merge queue gets slower with no attributable symptom — the failure this lane exists to make visible.
2026-09-10T14:28:03.7494023Z 
